            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0330" n="322" xml:id="pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">648T.006/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Nairobi</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bailey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nairobi</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-11-30T16:00:00+02:30">November 30, 1939—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 30—12:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of November 29, 6 p.m. Object of the import trade control is to
                    limit importation of nonessentials on account of available shipping and in order
                    to conserve exchange for essentials. Goods shipped to British East Africa before
                    November 15, goods for reexport outside British East Africa, sanction [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] importations in transit or for transshipment,
                    Government importations admissible without permission. Local importers
                    protesting. I believe American trade will suffer greatly under existing
                    circumstances.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bailey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
